From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dmcompos: composer (template from shape, segment from template/shape, transitions, AutoTransition), signpost track Compose

ComposeTemplateFromShape builds a template (a segment with a command track and a signpost track: groove levels by shape,
intro/end commands, a signpost per four measures, a cadence signpost for the ending). ComposeSegmentFromTemplate and
ComposeSegmentFromShape turn a template into a segment with the style, the style's tempo, the chord map, the commands and a
chord track made from the signposts (activity 0 to 3 sets how often the chord changes; measure length from the style's time
signature; fixed seed, so the result is deterministic). ComposeTransition composes a transition segment (command, long and
modulate flags, chords leading from the chord of the first segment to the first chord of the second); AutoTransition composes
it from what the performance plays and plays it, the destination following at its end. IDirectMusicTrack8::Compose of the
signpost track composes the chord track for the segment of the context (so IDirectMusicSegment8::Compose works).
The algorithm is this implementation's own; the documentation gives the interfaces and meanings, not the progression.
---
diff --git a/dlls/dmcompos/Makefile.in b/dlls/dmcompos/Makefile.in
index a95921c..1846855 100644
--- a/dlls/dmcompos/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/dmcompos/Makefile.in
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@ PARENTSRC = ../dmusic
 SOURCES = \
 	chordmap.c \
 	chordmaptrack.c \
+	compose.c \
 	composer.c \
 	dmcompos.idl \
 	dmcompos_main.c \
diff --git a/dlls/dmcompos/compose.c b/dlls/dmcompos/compose.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5d7f997
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/dmcompos/compose.c
@@ -0,0 +1,654 @@
+/* DirectMusic composer engine: templates from shapes, segments from templates, transitions
+ *
+ * A template is a segment with a command track (the groove levels and embellishments by measure)
+ * and a signpost track (where the chord progression goes through which chord). Composing a
+ * segment turns the signposts into a chord track. Everything is built from the data of the
+ * arguments and is deterministic: the pseudo random choices start from a fixed seed.
+ *
+ * The documentation gives the interfaces and the meaning of the shapes, activity levels and
+ * commands, not the algorithm: the grid of the progression (see the constants below) is this
+ * implementation's own.
+ *
